description=AMD FidelityFX (FSR) upscaling for Project Zomboid B42, one mod with two loading modes: EITHER add -javaagent pointing at this mod's single jar, 42\media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar, to the launch options (load-time agent, no extra mod needed), OR just keep ZombieBuddy (release 2.x or BETA 3.x) installed and enable this mod - ZombieBuddy loads the jar from mod.info and retransforms the game in place (first launch shows the ZombieBuddy approval dialog, choose persist). World pass renders at a reduced resolution (FidelityFX quality presets) and is resolved with FSR 1 EASU+RCAS, or FSR 2 / FSR 3.1 temporal upscaling (GL compute) with injected sub-pixel camera jitter, depth chain, auto-reactive masks and entity motion vectors, plus optional software frame generation on the present path (FsrControl.fsr2FgTest). Falls back to FSR 1 automatically on any compute fault. Running both modes at once is safe: the second entry detects the armed JVM and stands down. One jar serves both game builds in both modes: the runtime whitelist (AgentRev.SUPPORTED) accepts B42.22 (revision e013dbb529) and B42.21 (revision 4a0e9546ec, rollback). The single jar lives at media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar - the same file the javaagent launch option points at and ZombieBuddy loads through javaJarFile. Any other revision runs stock instead of transforming (runtime hash gate).

The single agent jar ships at media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar: the ZombieBuddy
mode loads it through mod.info (javaJarFile/javaPkgName) on game start, and
the javaagent launch option points at the same file. The runtime whitelist
(AgentRev.SUPPORTED) accepts B42.22 (e013dbb529) and B42.21 (4a0e9546ec), so
one jar serves both builds in both modes. Hook groups, downscale and upscaler
settings behave identically in both modes (ModOptions.ini / fsrupsc.FsrControl
from Lua).
